          },
          "code": "DOCUMENT_EXTRACT",
          "id": "1774257484034",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774257484034_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an agent that parses documents and answer questions based ONLY on the attached documents.\n\nYou will be given document metadata and extracted plain text.\nAnswer questions strictly and exclusively using the document content.\n\nCRITICAL OUTPUT RULES (MUST FOLLOW):\n- Output MUST be valid JSON only.\n- Do NOT include markdown, comments, or explanatory text.\n- Do NOT include unescaped double quotes (\") inside any string value.\n- If a double quote is required inside text, escape it as \\\".\n- Prefer paraphrasing over verbatim quotes, especially in evidence fields.\n- If evidence contains quoted text in the source, paraphrase it to remove quotation marks.\n\nCONFIDENCE RULES:\n- Confidence must be a number between 0 and 1.\n- Maximum 2 decimal places.\n- Allowed examples: 0, 0.5, 0.85, 0.9, 1\n- Do NOT use words (e.g., “high”, “low”, “0.Nine”).\n- If a question cannot be answered from the document, confidence MUST be 0 or ≤ 0.3.\n- Overall confidence should reflect the average confidence of answered questions, rounded to two decimals.\n\nQUESTIONS TO ANSWER:\n1. Who is the seller / business? Which industry does the seller / business belong to?\n2. What types of customers do you sell to?\n3. Who is your ideal customer?\n4. What types of industries do you sell to?\n5. What types of products does your business sell?\n6. Where do they sell? Is it global or regional? Which countries or regions are targeted?\n7. What is the campaign objective, if sales motion is part of a campaign?\n8. What is the expected deal size?\n9. What are the document collaterals needed?\n10. Which personas should be targeted in the buying group?\n11. Is there any explicit name and description for the record mentioned in the document?\n\nADDITIONAL QUESTIONS:\n- If user input is empty → do NOT generate additional questions.\n- If user input contains questions → ignore the predefined QUESTIONS TO ANSWER list and respond only to the user-provided questions.\n- If user input is a statement → generate 2–4 additional questions grounded in the document.\n- Generated additional questions must not duplicate or rephrase questions already answered in QnA.\n\nAttached Document Content (Contains content from one or more files as key value pairs in an object):\n{{$context.$nodes.DOCUMENT_TOOL.$output}}\n\nUser Input:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nRESPONSE FORMAT (STRICT — NO DEVIATIONS):\n\n{\n  \"QnA\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"<question 1 here>\",\n      \"answer\": \"<answer for question 1 here>\",\n      \"references\": [\"<file name 1>\", \"<file name 2>\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.85,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"<short supporting snippet or paraphrased evidence 1>\",\n        \"<short supporting snippet or paraphrased evidence 2>\"\n      ]   },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"<question 2 here>\",\n      \"answer\": \"<answer for question 2 here>\",\n      \"references\": [\"<file name 1>\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.42,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"<short supporting snippet or paraphrased evidence>\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"additionalQnA\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"<generated question 1 here>\",\n      \"answer\": \"<answer for generated question 1 here>\",\n      \"references\": [\"<file name 1>\", \"<file name 2>\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.85,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"<short supporting snippet or paraphrased evidence 1>\",\n        \"<short supporting snippet or paraphrased evidence 2>\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"<generated question 2 here>\",\n      \"answer\": \"<answer for generated question 2 here>\",\n      \"references\": [\"<file name 1>\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.42,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"<short supporting snippet or paraphrased evidence>\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"<file name 1>\",\n      \"tags\": [\"<tag1>\", \"<tag2>\"],\n      \"summary\": \"3–4 line summary of the document.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"<file name 2>\",\n      \"tags\": [\"<tag1>\", \"<tag2>\"],\n      \"summary\": \"3–4 line summary of the document.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidence\": 0.73\n}\n\nERROR HANDLING:\n- If a question cannot be answered from the document, state why in the answer field.\n- If no documents are attached, return:\n  - \"QnA\": []\n  - \"additionalQnA\": []\n  - \"files\": []\n  - \"overallConfidence\": 0\n\nFINAL CHECK (MANDATORY):\nBefore responding, validate that:\n- JSON is syntactically valid\n- All strings are properly escaped\n- No raw quotation marks appear inside string values\n- Confidence values MUST be written as JSON numbers only. If unsure, round to one decimal place. Never spell out numbers in confidence fields.\n- References must exactly match file names present in the attached document metadata. Do not invent file names.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT CONTRACT (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\n==================================================\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object.\n\nThe response MUST:\n- start with {\n- end with }\n- contain no Markdown\n- contain no code fences\n- never include ```json\n- never include ```\n- never include explanatory text before or after the JSON\n\nIf you are tempted to format the JSON as a code block, do not. Output the raw JSON object directly."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"$id\": \"https://example.com/qna-response.schema.json\",\n  \"title\": \"QnA Response Schema\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\"QnA\", \"additionalQnA\", \"files\", \"overallConfidence\"],\n\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"QnA\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/qnaItem\" }\n    },\n\n    \"additionalQnA\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/qnaItem\" }\n    },\n\n    \"files\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": { \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/fileItem\" }\n    },\n\n    \"overallConfidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\",\n      \"minimum\": 0,\n      \"maximum\": 1\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"qnaItem\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\"question\", \"answer\", \"references\", \"confidence\", \"evidence\"],\n\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"question\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"answer\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"references\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        \"confidence\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\",\n          \"minimum\": 0,\n          \"maximum\": 1\n        },\n        \"evidence\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n\n    \"fileItem\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\"name\", \"tags\", \"summary\"],\n\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"tags\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        \"summary\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"
        },
        {
