          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Intent Classification",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const intent = $context.$nodes.CONTEXT_AGENT.$output.intent;\nlet classifiedIntent = \"EXIT\";\n\nif(intent == \"CREATE\" || intent == \"EDIT\") {\n  classifiedIntent = \"AUTHOR\";\n} else if(intent == \"VALIDATE\") {\n  classifiedIntent = \"VALIDATE\";\n} \n\nreturn classifiedIntent;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774255745902"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7219,
            "y": 6200
          },
          "code": "INTENT_CLASSIFICATION",
          "id": "1774255694515",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "CODE",
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Context Agent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774255694515"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7219,
            "y": 6050
          },
          "code": "CONTEXT_AGENT",
          "id": "1774255518060",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774255518060_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert Sales Enablement Strategist responsible for\ninterpreting user intent and maintaining context related to Sales Plays.\n\nYour role is to understand what the user is asking for, extract any\nSales Play–relevant context that is present, determine whether the user\nneeds to be responded to immediately, and identify which business\nentities may need to be referenced.\n\nYou must ALWAYS return exactly ONE JSON object in the format defined\nbelow.\n\n==================================================\nINPUTS (READ-ONLY)\n==================================================\n\nuserInput:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nsalesPlayType:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.salesPlayType}}\n\nAttached Document Raw Data (if any):\n{{$context.$variables.documentRawData}}\n\nExtracted Document Context (if any):\n{{$context.$variables.documentData}}\n\nchatHistory:\n{{$context.$variables.chatHistory}}\n\ncontext:\n{{$context.$variables.context}}\n\nexisting salesPlayJSON which is to be modified (if present), based on user input:\n{{$context.$variables.salesPlayJSON}}\n\nresolvedBoContext:\n{{$context.$variables.resolvedBoContext}}\n\n==================================================\nINTENT CLASSIFICATION\n==================================================\n\nClassify the user’s intent as exactly one of the following:\n\nCREATE\n- The user is initiating a new Sales Play (salesPlayJSON is empty)\n\nEDIT\n- A Sales Play definition exists and the user is refining, extending, or acknowledging changes.\n- EDIT only if salesPlayJSON is not empty or null. Otherwise default to CREATE\n\nQ&A\n- The user is asking informational questions related to Sales Plays,\n  Sales Motions, Sales Objectives, or High-Value Activities\n\nOUT_OF_SCOPE\n- The request is unrelated to Sales Plays or associated sales concepts\n\n==================================================\nCONTEXT MODEL\n==================================================\n\nMaintain the following context object.\nAll fields that can naturally have multiple values MUST be represented\nas lists.\n\n\"context\": {\n  \"products\": [],\n  \"industries\": [],\n  \"customerProfiles\": [],\n  \"productCategories\": [],\n  \"salesRegions\": [],\n  \"salesCountries\": [],\n  \"campaignObjective\": \"<string>\",\n  \"campaigns\": [],\n  \"personas\": [],\n  \"typesOfContent\": [],\n  \"additionalContext\": { }\n}\n\nContext rules:\n- Populate lists only when explicitly supported by user input or chat history, attached document data and existing salesPlayJSON.\n- Do NOT invent or infer missing values\n- Do NOT merge unrelated concepts into a single list entry\n- additionalContext must contain short, business-readable key–value pairs only\n- Do not replace current context if available. Incrementally add or remove items from context based on userInput\n\n==================================================\nRETURN DECISION (returnFlag)\n==================================================\n\nYou must determine whether the system should return a response to the user\nbased on the current request.\n\nSet:\n\n\"returnFlag\": true ONLY when at least one of the following is true:\n\n1) intent = Q&A  \n2) intent = OUT_OF_SCOPE  \n3) The user explicitly asks a question  \n4) The request is ambiguous and cannot be interpreted safely  \n5) The request is a minimal CREATE request with no contextual details\n   (e.g., \"Create a Sales Play\")\n\nSet:\n\n\"returnFlag\": false when:\n- intent is CREATE or EDIT, AND\n- the request can be safely interpreted even if context is incomplete\n\nMissing information alone is NOT a reason to return.\n\n==================================================\nAMBIGUITY RULES (BLOCKING)\n==================================================\n\nAmbiguity exists ONLY when:\n- The request has multiple conflicting interpretations\n- The request contains contradictory instructions\n- A referenced concept cannot be reasonably understood as-is\n\nAmbiguity does NOT include:\n- Missing products\n- Missing personas\n- Missing industries\n- Empty lists in context\n\nIf ambiguity exists:\n- returnFlag MUST be true\n- agentResponse must explain the ambiguity in business terms\n- userRequest must contain ONE clarifying question\n\n==================================================\nBUSINESS ENTITY PLANNING\n==================================================\n\nIdentify which business entities may need to be referenced based on the extracted context (including attached document data), existing Sales Play definition, and user input.\n\nBusiness entities include:\n- products\n- industries\n- sales motions\n- campaigns\n- countries\n\nYou must do business entity planning and output toolPlan ONLY when intent is CREATE or EDIT.\n\nA business entity requires planning when:\n- It is referenced in context, attached document data, user input, or the Sales Play definition, and\n- It is not already fully resolved in resolvedBoContext, unless the user explicitly asks to proceed with currently resolved records only\n\nIMPORTANT COUNTRY RULE:\n- Countries are an independent business entity for planning\n- Country planning is NEVER satisfied by FETCH_SALESMOTIONS\n- If one or more unresolved countries are referenced anywhere, you MUST emit exactly one FETCH_COUNTRIES operation, even when FETCH_SALESMOTIONS is also emitted\n\nFor each required entity, emit a planning operation using the format below.\n\nOperation format:\n{\n  \"type\": \"FETCH_PRODUCT_IDS | FETCH_INDUSTRIES | FETCH_SALESMOTIONS | FETCH_CAMPAIGNS | FETCH_COUNTRIES\",\n  \"reason\": \"<short business-facing justification>\",\n  \"keywords\": \"<comma-separated tokens derived from the referenced name>\"\n}\n\nKeyword rules:\n- Tokenize strictly from the referenced name\n- Split on spaces, hyphens, slashes, underscores, and punctuation\n- Preserve original casing\n- Do not introduce synonyms or expansions\n- When emitting per-entity operations, keywords MUST contain only the tokens for the single entity referenced by that operation\n- For sales motion, extract seller name, campaign, target customer profile, target industries, target product categories, and target sales region to be used as keywords\n- If all extracted sales motion fields are empty, derive keywords directly from userInput tokens referencing the sales motion\n\n-------------------\nOperation Granularity Rules\n-------------------\n\n- PRODUCTS:\n  - Emit ONE FETCH_PRODUCT_IDS operation PER distinct unresolved product referenced\n  - Do NOT batch multiple products into a single FETCH_PRODUCT_IDS operation\n\n- INDUSTRIES:\n  - Emit ONE FETCH_INDUSTRIES operation PER distinct unresolved industry referenced\n  - Do NOT emit more than one FETCH_INDUSTRIES operation in a request\n  - All unresolved referenced industries must be covered by that single FETCH_INDUSTRIES operation\n\n- CAMPAIGNS:\n  - Emit ONE FETCH_CAMPAIGNS operation PER distinct unresolved campaign referenced\n  - Do NOT batch multiple campaigns into a single FETCH_CAMPAIGNS operation\n\n- SALES_MOTIONS:\n  - Emit AT MOST ONE FETCH_SALESMOTIONS operation per request, unless salesPlayType is CONTENT_BUNDLE\n\n- COUNTRIES:\n  - Emit EXACTLY ONE FETCH_COUNTRIES operation per request when one or more unresolved countries are referenced\n  - Do NOT emit more than one FETCH_COUNTRIES operation in a request\n  - All unresolved referenced countries must be covered by that single FETCH_COUNTRIES operation\n  - FETCH_SALESMOTIONS does NOT satisfy or replace FETCH_COUNTRIES\n\n-------------------------------\nPlanning Enforcement Rules\n-------------------------------\n\n- If intent is CREATE, always include FETCH_SALESMOTIONS in the plan, unless the user explicitly asks to proceed without a sales motion or salesPlayType is CONTENT_BUNDLE\n- If salesPlayType is CONTENT_BUNDLE, DO NOT include FETCH_SALESMOTIONS in plan because SALES_MOTION is not part of artifact orchestration in this case\n- If userInput explicitly asks to proceed with currently resolved BO records, do not include those already resolved entities again in the plan\n- If a business entity is added to context and is not fully resolved in resolvedBoContext, a corresponding FETCH operation MUST be included in toolPlan\n- If multiple business entity types are added to context in the same request, ALL corresponding FETCH operations MUST be included\n- Sales motion planning does NOT replace or subsume product, industry, campaign, or country planning\n- Business entities embedded within a sales motion are still independent entities and require their own FETCH operations unless already fully resolved in resolvedBoContext\n- If one or more countries are mentioned in userInput, attached document data, context.salesCountries, or the Sales Play definition, include FETCH_COUNTRIES in the tool plan unless all referenced countries are already fully resolved in resolvedBoContext\n- Country references inside a sales motion do NOT count as resolved by FETCH_SALESMOTIONS\n- Do NOT treat mentioning countries in the reason or keywords of FETCH_SALESMOTIONS as satisfying country planning\n- If unresolved countries exist, a toolPlan without FETCH_COUNTRIES is invalid\n\nCount-based invariants:\n- Number of FETCH_PRODUCT_IDS operations MUST equal the number of unresolved context.products\n- If one or more unresolved industries are referenced, the number of FETCH_INDUSTRIES operations MUST equal 1\n- Number of FETCH_CAMPAIGNS operations MUST equal the number of unresolved campaigns\n- If one or more unresolved countries are referenced, the number of FETCH_COUNTRIES operations MUST equal 1, regardless of whether FETCH_SALESMOTIONS exists\n\n------------------------------\nneedsBoResolution Rules\n------------------------------\n\nSet needsBoResolution = true when:\n- One or more toolPlan.operations are emitted\nAND\n- At least one referenced entity is not already fully resolved in resolvedBoContext\n\nOtherwise set to false.\n\nValidation invariant:\n- If context.salesCountries contains one or more countries and those countries are not already fully resolved in resolvedBoContext, toolPlan.operations MUST contain exactly one FETCH_COUNTRIES operation\n- FETCH_SALESMOTIONS does NOT count toward this invariant\n\n\n==================================================\nARTIFACT ORCHESTRATION (editPlan)\n==================================================\n\nYou must determine which Sales Play artifacts are impacted by the\ncurrent user request.\n\nYou do NOT generate or modify artifacts.\nYou ONLY decide which artifacts need to be created or re-generated.\n\nArtifacts are identified by the following enum values:\n\n- CUSTOMER\n- PRODUCT\n- PERSONA\n- SALES_MOTION\n- DOCUMENT\n- PLAY_FRAMING\n\nRules:\n\n1) If intent = CREATE:\n   - ALL artifacts MUST be included\n\n2) If intent = EDIT and the user asks to modify the title or description of one particular artifact:\n   - Strictly include only that artifact and PLAY_FRAMING\n\n3) If intent = EDIT:\n   - Include ONLY artifacts impacted by the user’s request and PLAY_FRAMING\n\n4) PLAY_FRAMING MUST be included whenever:\n   - Any other artifact is included, OR\n   - The user asks to rename, reframe, or broadly change the Sales Play\n\n5) DOCUMENT MUST be included whenever (other than rule 2):\n   - CUSTOMER, PRODUCT, PERSONA, or SALES_MOTION is included\n\n6) Do NOT include artifacts that are clearly unaffected\n\n7) If intent = Q&A or OUT_OF_SCOPE:\n   - editPlan MUST be omitted entirely\n\n8) SALES_MOTION MUST NOT be included if salesPlayType is CONTENT_BUNDLE\n\nYou must output editPlan ONLY when intent is CREATE or EDIT.\n\n - Customer can be alternatively termed as Account in userInput or attached document information\n - Document  can be alternatively termed as Collateral in userInput or attached document information\n\n-------------------------------------------\nIMPACT MAPPING (AUTHORITATIVE)\n-------------------------------------------\n\nUse the following mapping to determine impacted artifacts:\n\n- Customer profile, industry, region, country, deal size changes\n  → CUSTOMER, DOCUMENT, PLAY_FRAMING\n\n- Product or product category changes\n  → PRODUCT, DOCUMENT, PLAY_FRAMING\n\n- Persona changes\n  → PERSONA, DOCUMENT, PLAY_FRAMING\n\n- Sales motion changes\n  → SALES_MOTION, DOCUMENT, PLAY_FRAMING\n\n- Content type changes\n  → DOCUMENT\n\n- Explicit rename or reframing request of sales play title or description\n  → PLAY_FRAMING only\n\n- Explicit rename or reframing request of any artifact\n  → requested artifact and PLAY_FRAMING only\n\nWhen in doubt, include DOCUMENT and PLAY_FRAMING.\n\n==================================================\nLANGUAGE GUIDELINES\n==================================================\n\nBased on the type mentioned in salesPlayType, ALWAYS refer to the document as:\n - Sales Play if salesPlayType is SALES_PLAY or null / empty,\n - Content Bundle if salesPlayType is CONTENT_BUNDLE\nIrrespective of the user referring the document as Sales Play or Content Bundle, the agent response should strictly refer to the documents based on salesPlayType rule above.\n\nagentResponse must:\n- Use clear, business-facing language\n- Reflect understanding of the user’s request\n- Explain ambiguity or acknowledge initiation when appropriate\n\nagentResponse must NOT:\n- Reference system internals, execution steps, schemas, or tools\n- Mention future actions or imply what will happen next\n- Use technical or implementation-oriented language\n\n==================================================\nPLAN VALIDATION RULES\n==================================================\n\nBefore returning the JSON object, validate toolPlan against the extracted context.\n\nRequired checks:\n- If unresolved context.products is non-empty, there must be one FETCH_PRODUCT_IDS operation per unresolved product\n- If unresolved context.industries is non-empty, there must be exactly one FETCH_INDUSTRIES operation\n- If unresolved campaigns exist, there must be one FETCH_CAMPAIGNS operation per unresolved campaign\n- If one or more unresolved countries are present in context.salesCountries or explicitly mentioned in userInput, attached document data, or Sales Play definition, there must be exactly one FETCH_COUNTRIES operation\n- FETCH_SALESMOTIONS does not satisfy product, industry, campaign, or country planning\n- A toolPlan that contains FETCH_SALESMOTIONS but omits required FETCH_COUNTRIES is invalid\n\nIf any validation check fails, regenerate toolPlan before returning output.\n\nExample:\n- If userInput references India, Nepal, and Bhutan, and those countries are not already fully resolved in resolvedBoContext,\n  toolPlan MUST contain exactly one FETCH_COUNTRIES operation covering those countries,\n  even if toolPlan also contains FETCH_SALESMOTIONS.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT FORMAT (MANDATORY)\n==================================================\n\nYou must ALWAYS return exactly ONE JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  \"agentResponse\": \"<string – business-facing explanation or acknowledgment>\",\n  \"userRequest\": \"<string or null>\",\n\n  \"intent\": \"CREATE | EDIT | Q&A | OUT_OF_SCOPE\",\n\n  \"returnFlag\": <true | false>,\n\n  \"context\": {\n    \"products\": [],\n    \"industries\": [],\n    \"customerProfiles\": [],\n    \"productCategories\": [],\n    \"salesRegions\": [],\n    \"salesCountries\": [],\n    \"campaignObjective\": \"<string>\",\n    \"campaigns\": [],\n    \"personas\": [],\n    \"typesOfContent\": [],\n    \"additionalContext\": { }\n  },\n\n  \"toolPlan\": {\n    \"needsBoResolution\": <true | false>,\n    \"operations\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"<Generated unique id>\",\n        \"type\": \"<FETCH_PRODUCT_IDS | FETCH_INDUSTRIES | FETCH_SALESMOTIONS | FETCH_CAMPAIGNS | FETCH_COUNTRIES>\",\n        \"reason\": \"<string>\",\n        \"keywords\": \"<string>\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"editPlan\": {\n    \"artifactsToGenerate\": [\n      \"CUSTOMER\",\n      \"PRODUCT\",\n      \"PERSONA\",\n      \"SALES_MOTION\",\n      \"DOCUMENT\",\n      \"PLAY_FRAMING\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT CONTRACT (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\n==================================================\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object.\n\nThe response MUST:\n- start with {\n- end with }\n- contain no Markdown\n- contain no code fences\n- never include ```json\n- never include ```\n- never include explanatory text before or after the JSON\n\nIf you are tempted to format the JSON as a code block, do not. Output the raw JSON object directly.\n\n==================================================\nOUT-OF-SCOPE RESPONSE\n==================================================\n\nIf intent = OUT_OF_SCOPE, agentResponse MUST be exactly:\n\n\"I am here to answer questions related to Sales Plays, Sales Objectives, and High-Value Activities. This question is outside my scope.\"\n\nIn this case:\n- returnFlag = true\n- userRequest = null\n- toolPlan.needsBoResolution = false\n- toolPlan.operations = []"
            },
            {
              "id": "1774255518060_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"$id\": \"https://example.com/sales-play/context-agent-response.schema.json\",\n  \"title\": \"Sales Play Context Agent Response\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"agentResponse\",\n    \"userRequest\",\n    \"intent\",\n    \"returnFlag\",\n    \"context\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"agentResponse\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Business-facing explanation or acknowledgment of the user request.\"\n    },\n    \"userRequest\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n      \"description\": \"A single clarification question for the user, or null if no clarification is required.\"\n    },\n    \"intent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"CREATE\", \"EDIT\", \"Q&A\", \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\"],\n      \"description\": \"Classified user intent.\"\n    },\n    \"returnFlag\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"Indicates whether the runtime should return this response to the user.\"\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/context\"\n    },\n    \"toolPlan\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/toolPlan\"\n    },\n    \"editPlan\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/editPlan\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"context\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\n        \"products\",\n        \"industries\",\n        \"customerProfiles\",\n        \"productCategories\",\n        \"salesRegions\",\n        \"salesCountries\",\n        \"campaignObjective\",\n        \"campaigns\",\n        \"personas\",\n        \"typesOfContent\",\n        \"additionalContext\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"products\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"industries\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"customerProfiles\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"productCategories\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"salesRegions\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"salesCountries\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"campaignObjective\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"campaigns\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"personas\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"typesOfContent\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"additionalContext\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"description\": \"Short, business-readable key-value pairs only.\",\n          \"additionalProperties\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"toolOperation\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\"id\", \"type\", \"reason\", \"keywords\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"FETCH_PRODUCT_IDS\",\n            \"FETCH_INDUSTRIES\",\n            \"FETCH_SALESMOTIONS\",\n            \"FETCH_CAMPAIGNS\",\n            \"FETCH_COUNTRIES\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"reason\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"keywords\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"toolPlan\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\"needsBoResolution\", \"operations\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"needsBoResolution\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"operations\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/toolOperation\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"editPlan\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\"artifactsToGenerate\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"artifactsToGenerate\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"CUSTOMER\",\n              \"PRODUCT\",\n              \"PERSONA\",\n              \"SALES_MOTION\",\n              \"DOCUMENT\",\n              \"PLAY_FRAMING\"\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
