          },
          "code": "AUTHOR_ARTIFACTS",
          "id": "1774255861131",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774255861131_collection",
              "name": "collection",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.SPLIT_ARTIFACTS.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LOOP"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Validate BO resolution"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774258425502"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7469,
            "y": 8187.557869712096
          },
          "code": "VALIDATE_BO_RESOLUTION",
          "id": "1774258402045",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774258402045_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert Sales Enablement Strategist responsible for confirming user intent when a resolved Business Object (BO) does not fully align with the request.\n\nInputs:\n- User input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- salesPlayType: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.salesPlayType}}\n- Extracted context: {{$context.$nodes.CONTEXT_AGENT.$output.context}}\n- BO resolution output: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_BO_CONTEXT.$output.result}}\n\nYour task:\n1. Inspect each BO resolution entry independently.\n2. Evaluate alignment using ONLY the result.items array.\n3. Ignore all metadata such as hasMore, count, offset, limit, scores, or timestamps.\n4. Identify ONLY BO entries where the resolved item does not fully align with the user’s stated intent.\n5. For those BOs:\n   - State which record(s) were identified by the tool operation\n   - State how their scope differs from the user request\n6. Ask the user to either confirm use of the identified record(s) or specify a different intent.\n\nAlignment rules (items-only):\nA BO requires confirmation if:\n- No item was resolved\n- More than one item was resolved\n- A resolved item has a scope mismatch with the user request (e.g., region, segment, audience)\n\nA BO does NOT require confirmation if:\n- Exactly one item is resolved AND\n- Its scope reasonably matches the user request\n\nFETCH_SALESMOTIONS-specific rules:\n- Match user input and extracted context to the BO output for customer profile, industry, product category, and sales region.\n- Only mark ambiguous when the resolved item explicitly contradicts the user input or extracted context.\n- Do NOT mark ambiguous due to missing data in the resolved Sales Motion output (e.g., persona, campaign objectives).\n\nCritical response constraints:\n- Do NOT suggest adapting, modifying, or creating records\n- Do NOT propose alternative system actions\n- Do NOT reference tools, resolution logic, or internal checks\n- Do NOT mention BOs that fully align\n- Do NOT list options using A/B/C or numbered choices\n- Do NOT include questions in agentResponse\n- When referring to resolved records, describe them as \"matched\" or \"identified\".\n- Do NOT describe records as \"picked\", \"selected\", \"chosen\", or imply system-side decision-making.\n\nMulti-BO handling:\n- If multiple BOs require confirmation, combine them into a single declarative agentResponse that states each identified record and how its scope differs from the user request.\n\nOutput format (JSON only):\n{\n  \"agentResponse\": \"<declarative statement describing the identified record(s) and scope mismatch>\",\n  \"userRequest\": \"<exactly one confirmation or re-specification question>\",\n  \"ambiguityFound\": <true | false>,\n  \"ambiguityDetails\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"<tool operation id>\",\n      \"type\": \"<tool type>\",\n      \"ambiguityReason\": \"<reason the resolved item contradicts the user input or context>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT CONTRACT (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\n==================================================\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object.\n\nThe response MUST:\n- start with {\n- end with }\n- contain no Markdown\n- contain no code fences\n- never include ```json\n- never include ```\n- never include explanatory text before or after the JSON\n\nIf you are tempted to format the JSON as a code block, do not. Output the raw JSON object directly.\n\n==================================================\nLANGUAGE GUIDELINES\n==================================================\n\nBased on the type mentioned in salesPlayType, ALWAYS refer to the document as:\n - Sales Play if salesPlayType is SALES_PLAY or null / empty,\n - Content Bundle if salesPlayType is CONTENT_BUNDLE\nIrrespective of the user referring the document as Sales Play or Content Bundle, the agent response should strictly refer to the documents based on salesPlayType rule above.\n\nagentResponse must:\n- Be a declarative statement\n- State what was identified as a fact\n- Mention only BOs that require confirmation\n\nuserRequest must:\n- Contain exactly one question\n- Ask whether to proceed with the identified record(s) or specify a different intent\n- Avoid implying system-side changes"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"title\": \"BO Clarification Agent Output\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"agentResponse\",\n    \"userRequest\",\n    \"ambiguityFound\",\n    \"ambiguityDetails\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"agentResponse\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Declarative statement describing the matched BO record and any scope mismatch. Must not be a question.\",\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"pattern\": \"^[^?]*$\"\n    },\n    \"userRequest\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Single clarification question asking the user to confirm the matched record or specify a different intent.\",\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"pattern\": \"\\\\?$\"\n    },\n    \"ambiguityFound\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"Indicates whether user clarification is required due to BO misalignment.\"\n    },\n    \"ambiguityDetails\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"Detailed list of ambiguity per tool operation.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"required\": [\"id\", \"type\", \"ambiguityReason\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"FETCH_PRODUCT_IDS\",\n              \"FETCH_INDUSTRIES\",\n              \"FETCH_SALESMOTIONS\",\n              \"FETCH_CAMPAIGNS\"\n            ],\n            \"description\": \"Type of business entity resolution required.\"\n          },\n          \"ambiguityReason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Ambiguity reason for the operation.\"\n          },\n          \"keywords\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Comma-separated tokens derived from referenced names.\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Parse Artifacts",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const artifactStringArray = $context.$nodes.AUTHOR_ARTIFACTS.$output;\nconst artifacts = []\nlet authoringResponse = {};\n\nfor(let stringObject of artifactStringArray) {\n  const artifactObject = JSON.parse(stringObject);\n  if(artifactObject.hasOwnProperty(\"type\")) {\n    artifacts.push(artifactObject);\n  } else {authoringResponse = artifactObject}\n}\n\n// Add back unmodified artifacts\n\nconst intent = $context.$nodes.CONTEXT_AGENT.$output.intent;\nconst artifactsToGenerate = $context.$nodes.CONTEXT_AGENT.$output.editPlan.artifactsToGenerate;\n\nconst currentArtifacts =\n  $context.$variables.salesPlayJSON?.artifacts === undefined ||\n  $context.$variables.salesPlayJSON?.artifacts === null ||\n  $context.$variables.salesPlayJSON?.artifacts === \"\"\n    ? []\n    : $context.$variables.salesPlayJSON?.artifacts;\n\nfor (let i = 0; i < currentArtifacts.length; i++) {\n  if(!artifactsToGenerate.includes(currentArtifacts[i].type)) {\n    artifacts.push(currentArtifacts[i]);\n  }\n}\n\nconst response = {authoringResponse, artifacts};\nreturn response;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774256818118"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7469,
            "y": 10250
          },
          "code": "PARSE_ARTIFACTS",
          "id": "1774256782037",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "CODE",
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Update BO Context",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const resolvedBoContext =\n  $context.$nodes.PREPARE_BO_CONTEXT.$output.result;\n\nconst ambiguityDetails =\n  $context.$nodes.VALIDATE_BO_RESOLUTION.$output.ambiguityDetails;\n\n// Build lookup: id → ambiguity object\nconst ambiguityMap = ambiguityDetails.reduce((acc, item) => {\n  acc[item.id] = item;\n  return acc;\n}, {});\n\n// Merge + flag\nconst mergedBoContext = resolvedBoContext.map(item => {\n  const ambiguity = ambiguityMap[item.id];\n\n  return {\n    ...item,\n    ambiguityFound: Boolean(ambiguity),\n    ...(ambiguity && { ambiguityReason: ambiguity.ambiguityReason })\n  };\n});\n\nreturn mergedBoContext;",
            "description": "Update Resolved BO Context"
          },
          "outcomes": {
